From 50d6f8d7e1f65de798ec9e3a95362a6de969f1e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Parsonage <eric@eparsonage.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:41:13 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Read imports from open editor buffers

Analysis read every imported module from disk, so an unsaved change to an
open dependency had no effect on the documents that require it. A compiled
file in the project could also keep a macro expansion older than its
source.

Give each analysis attempt the open buffers as an immutable table. An
import with an open buffer reads that buffer, and modules below a
workspace folder or the directory of an open buffer load from source.
Installed collections keep compiled loading. The controller records the
module files each accepted analysis loaded and analyses those documents
again when one of those buffers opens, changes or closes. A result that
read a buffer which has since changed is discarded and analysed again.
